From e5f162258e3ee98ce0b990ed83a4fb4feef0c61b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Inventory: 16-bit item ids in RAM, u8 in the v1 save
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step 3 of docs/mods/ids.md (§ 10), the inventory.

- INVENTORY.types is ItemId[30]; an empty slot is ITEM_NONE (-1) instead
  of 0xFF, so 255 is an item like any other. giveItem, removeItem and
  getItemCount take an ItemId; their logic is unchanged.
- The save payload keeps the v1 layout through SavedInventory; loading
  maps 0xFF to ITEM_NONE and saving writes the low byte (ITEM_NONE becomes
  0xFF again), so saves are byte-identical while ids are < 255.
- u8 sources keep their meaning through itemFromLegacy (0xFF = none): the
  initial inventory, GIVE_ITEM/REMOVE_ITEM and the IF item condition.
- The inventory menu (names, sprites, descriptions, move, sort) works on
  ItemId; sortItemsById/copyItemArray/swapItemId are 16-bit.
- FISH_renderBaitMenu read the amounts as types + 0x1E (one array past
  types); it now reads amounts directly, which also works with 16-bit
  types.

Shop, Item Keeper and recycle lists are still u8 (ITEM_MENU buffers);
they change with ITEM.DAT (step 7).

